## TODO: source-identity-refactor

Phase 2 of the multi-source expansion. Do AFTER nexus-prototype-merge. This is the
change that gets harder the longer it waits, because it touches persisted user
state (.modrex.json).

### Context

Mod identity today is a bare number in one global namespace: `InstalledMod.id` is
"the modworkshop remote id", negative = unidentified (and, post-merge, negative =
nexus by convention). Everything keys on it: modCache/filesCache/linksCache,
dismissedDepsWarnings, loaderModIds, hardcoded loader ids (SuperBLT-family
53474/14267, UE4SS 44048/47771/47749, Menu Backgrounds host 17160), useModData
dedupe, installedByModId, host-pack `location: "host:<id>:<subpath>"`, uid schemes
`{file_id}` / `{file_id}_{entry_stem}`. Two sources collide on ids immediately.
Steam Workshop PublishedFileId is a 64-bit integer that OVERFLOWS JavaScript's
safe-integer range - remote ids must become STRINGS in TS, not numbers.

### What to do

- Identity becomes the pair `(source: string, remoteId: string)` everywhere a mod
  is referenced. `InstalledMod.source` already exists (serde default
  "modworkshop") - start consuming it instead of special-casing.
- State migration in reconcile_state (the established migration point - see the
  .pd3mm.json and legacy-.disabled migrations there for the pattern): modworkshop
  entries get source stamped by the serde default already; nexus entries recover
  `(source="nexus", remoteId, fileRemoteId)` by parsing the
  `nexus:{mod}:{file}` uid. After migration, delete the negative-id-means-nexus
  convention and the `source == "nexus"` guards in identify.rs and
  installedUtils.ts. Negative id goes back to meaning exactly one thing:
  unidentified.
- Cache keys in the renderer become source-qualified: modCache/filesCache/
  linksCache/installedMetaCache (`modCache.ts`), browseCache (already keyed by
  workshopId - generalize the key to `(source, gameRef, ...)`), thumbnail cache
  keys (see thumbnails note in sources-module-restructure).
- dismissedDepsWarnings, loaderModIds, and the hardcoded loader-id tables in
  deps.ts get source-qualified or explicitly scoped modworkshop-only (loaders ARE
  modworkshop-hosted today; scoping is fine, silent ambiguity is not).
- uid scheme for new installs becomes source-prefixed for every source (the nexus
  branch already does `nexus:{mod}:{file}`; modworkshop keeps `{file_id}` /
  `{file_id}_{entry_stem}` for backward compat - do NOT rewrite existing uids,
  they are stable identity).
- Version/update semantics: replace the magic version strings "unknown"/"outdated"
  with an explicit updateStatus enum on the domain side while in here, or schedule
  it with mod-source-domain-model - per-source version semantics (Nexus semverish,
  Steam timestamps, modworkshop two version fields) do not fit one string field.

