# Architecture review 2026-07-17 (all gated on nexus-prototype-merge)

The entries below came out of a full architecture/security/performance review on
2026-07-17. EVERY entry in this section is blocked on `nexus-prototype-merge` and must
NOT be started until the `feature/nexus-prototype` branch is merged to main. The reason
is concrete, not cautious: the Nexus branch touches ~39 files / +3133 lines, heavily in
lib.rs, api.ts, types.ts, App.tsx, SettingsPage.tsx, Sidebar.tsx, mods/mod.rs,
identify.rs, and types.rs - which are exactly the files most of this work rewrites. Doing
any of it before the merge multiplies rebase conflicts on a branch that is itself gated
on an external dependency (the Nexus support team, via email). Note also that the Nexus
branch ALREADY fixed the `open_url` cmd-metacharacter finding (it switched to rundll32);
do not re-address that.

Recommended post-merge order (each makes the next cheaper):
typed-ipc-codegen -> typed-install-results -> backend-state-lock ->
game-registry (+ loader-registry) -> the rest. index-lookup-connection-reuse,
extract-deps-check-hook, and ci-security-and-invariant-checks are independent and can
slot in whenever. modrex-core-crate and plugin-system are far-future, each with its own
additional trigger.

---

## TODO: index-lookup-connection-reuse

Performance. Small (~1h). Post-nexus only because identify.rs is lightly touched by the
branch - do it right after merge to avoid a trivial conflict.

### The problem

`upgrade_negative_ids` (src-tauri/src/commands/mods/identify.rs, ~line 180) loops every
unidentified installed mod and calls `mod_index::lookup_sha256`, then on a miss
`mod_index::lookup_by_name`. Both PUBLIC wrappers (mod_index.rs ~line 277 and ~286)
REOPEN index.db from disk on every call via `open_conn`. So N unidentified mods cause up
to 2N SQLite file-opens. This runs inside `get_installed`, which fires at startup, on
every window focus (500ms debounce), and after every path change - a hot path.

The sibling pass already does it right: `identify_untracked` opens the connection ONCE
via `mod_index::open_index` (mods/mod.rs ~line 224) and passes the shared
`&rusqlite::Connection` to the private `query_sha256` / `query_by_name` helpers.

### The fix

- In `upgrade_negative_ids`, open the index once at the top (`mod_index::open_index(app)`),
  return early if None (index absent - same as today's implicit per-call existence check),
  then call the private `mod_index::query_sha256(&conn, sha, game_name)` /
  `query_by_name(&conn, name, game_name)` inside the loop instead of the reopening public
  wrappers. Those private helpers are already `pub(crate)` and take `&Connection`.
- Check the other caller of `lookup_sha256` first: get_installed's host-pack recovery loop
  (mods/mod.rs ~line 140) also calls it per discovered host pack. Either hoist the same
  single connection there too, or leave it (host packs are rare). Do not remove the public
  wrappers unless this was their last use.
- Pure I/O reduction, no behavior change. Existing mod_index_tests already cover the query
  functions; add nothing unless you change a signature.

---

## TODO: typed-ipc-codegen

Reliability foundation. Medium-Large. Blocked on: nexus-prototype-merge (touches every
command signature plus lib.rs/api.ts/types.ts - the branch's hottest files - and must
cover the new nexus/nxm/oauth commands). DO THIS FIRST of the post-merge architecture
work; typed-install-results and the source-* refactors build on a typed surface.

### The problem

The Rust<->TS wire contract is maintained BY HAND in two places: the serde structs in
src-tauri (rename_all camelCase) and the interfaces in src/shared/types.ts.
`pnpm check-commands` (scripts/check-commands.mjs, pre-commit + CI) enforces that command
NAMES and arity line up between `generate_handler!` (lib.rs) and the `invoke(...)` calls
(api.ts) - but it does NOT verify payload SHAPES. Rename or retype a struct field on one
side without mirroring it and both sides compile while the channel breaks at runtime.
Confirmed there is no codegen today (no ts-rs/specta/typeshare in Cargo.toml).

### The fix

- Adopt `tauri-specta` + `specta`. Derive `specta::Type` on command param/return structs
  and enums; collect commands via `tauri_specta::Builder`; emit a generated TS module
  (e.g. src/renderer/src/bindings.ts) at build time.
- api.ts stays the single IPC boundary (the renderer.md invariant) - it imports the
  generated typed functions instead of hand-writing `invoke` string names.
- src/shared/types.ts: replace hand-written WIRE types with re-exports of the generated
  types. Keep renderer-only VIEW types (things never sent over IPC) separate and hand-written.
- Replace or augment check-commands.mjs with a CI "generated bindings are up to date"
  git-diff check (mirror the check-licenses job pattern in ci.yml: regenerate, `git diff
  --exit-code`).
- DOMAIN vs WIRE caveat: this codegen encodes the CURRENT modworkshop-shaped wire types.
  The later mod-source-domain-model TODO replaces those with neutral domain types. Do
  typed-ipc-codegen first (mechanical), then domain-model on top of an already-typed surface.

### Verification

Full `pnpm typecheck` + `pnpm test`, then smoke-run the app (get_installed, an install, a
browse fetch) to confirm no serialization regressions - specta camelCase/rename settings
must match the existing serde rename_all exactly or every field silently mismatches.

---

## TODO: typed-install-results

Reliability. Large. Blocked on: typed-ipc-codegen (and therefore nexus-prototype-merge).

### The problem

Install commands signal "this archive needs a user decision" by returning `Err(String)`
whose text is a sentinel-prefixed JSON blob: `ZIP_MULTI_PAK:{...}`, `HOST_MOD_PACK:{...}`,
`CB_FLAT_ARCHIVE:{...}`, `UNRECOGNIZED_ARCHIVE:{...}` (produced by
`resolve_archive_download` / `classify_archive_dirs` in mods/zip.rs; plus an internal
`UE4SS_LOADER:` sentinel handled entirely in Rust). The renderer parses these out of the
error string in every install entry point's catch block via `handleInstallSentinel`
(src/renderer/src/installSentinels.ts) + `parseZipMultiPak` / `parseHostModPack` /
`parseCbFlatArchive` / `isUnrecognizedArchive`. This is an untyped protocol on the ERROR
channel. CLAUDE.md/renderer.md record two real regressions from an entry point forgetting
a sentinel (the reinstall path, then the Updates modal), each surfacing a raw `**:{...}`
string to the user.

### The fix

- Rust: model the result as a typed discriminated union in the Ok channel, e.g.
  `enum InstallOutcome { Installed, NeedsPicker(ZipMultiPakPayload),
  NeedsHostChoice(HostPackPayload), NeedsCbFlatConfirm(CbFlatPayload),
  Unrecognized(UnrecognizedPayload) }` (specta::Type, typed end-to-end via
  typed-ipc-codegen). Genuine failures stay `Err`.
- Renderer: replace catch-block sentinel parsing with an exhaustive `switch` on the typed
  outcome. TypeScript exhaustiveness then makes "handle all cases" a COMPILE error if an
  entry point misses one - this eliminates the exact regression class the prose invariant
  currently guards.
- Migrate ALL entry points (that is the point): BrowsePage.handleInstall,
  ModDetailPage.handleInstall + DownloadsTab, InstalledPage reinstall
  (useModActions.handleReinstall), UpdatesModal, FileSelectModal.
- Nexus tie-in: the branch's install_nexus_download currently returns an honest error for
  these sentinels because the picker modals are modworkshop-shaped. This refactor is where
  Nexus installs return the same typed outcomes so the pickers work for Nexus too
  (coordinate with the nexus-prototype-merge sentinel-story decision).

---

## TODO: backend-state-lock

Reliability. Medium. Blocked on: nexus-prototype-merge (the branch adds new install entry
points in mods/mod.rs that must be covered).

### The problem

Concurrent writes to a game's `.modrex.json` are prevented today by RENDERER discipline:
the `isRefreshingInstalled` ref in App.tsx stops two `get_installed` calls racing, and
callers are expected to serialize. `save_state` (mods/state.rs) is atomic PER WRITE (temp
+ rename), but there is no backend mutual exclusion, so two commands that read-modify-write
state (e.g. an install firing while a focus-triggered get_installed reconciles) can
interleave and lose updates - the exact race the renderer guard papers over. With one UI
caller it is survivable; with Nexus deep-link installs (nxm:// can fire while the UI is
doing something else) and any future automation/CLI/plugin caller, renderer discipline is
not enough.

### The fix

- Add a PER-GAME async lock in managed Tauri state (e.g. a
  `Mutex<HashMap<String, Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex<()>>>>` keyed by game_id, or a
  single-writer task per game). Every state-mutating command acquires the game's lock for
  the read-modify-write span: install_mod, install_file, install_from_zip_entry,
  install_cb_flat_archive, install_host_pack, uninstall_mod, enable_mod, disable_mod,
  move_crimeboss_mod_target, the folder ops (create/rename/delete/move/reorder), and
  get_installed's reconcile-and-save tail.
- Per-game, so operations on different games stay parallel.
- CRITICAL: do not hold the lock across the network download in install_mod/install_file.
  Download to temp first, acquire the lock only for the disk-write + state-update phase, or
  a slow download serializes unrelated installs.
- Leave the renderer's `isRefreshingInstalled` guard in place as a cheap client-side
  debounce; update its comment to say the backend is now authoritative. Do not remove it in
  the same change.

---

## TODO: game-registry

Scalability. Medium (Stages 1+3 are behavior-preserving). Blocked on:
nexus-prototype-merge (conflicts with the branch's App.tsx/SettingsPage/Sidebar/types.ts
edits, and the registry should absorb the Nexus per-game `nexusDomain` axis in one pass
rather than being reshaped twice). This SUPERSEDES the "do not act now" note at the bottom
of kill-pd3-fallback: the owner decided on 2026-07-17 to pursue game-count scalability
toward 20-100+ games.

### The problem (measured)

Adding one game touches ~15 wiring files. Measured against the RAID merge
(feat/raid-ww2-support): 25 files / ~530 insertions, of which ~10 are irreducible (novel
behavior + tests + docs) and ~15 are pure wiring. Game identity is restated in many
places: launchers/games/<game>.rs (`GameDef`), launchers/games/mod.rs (registration),
launchers/mod.rs (`game_def_for_id` dispatch arm), mods/engine.rs (the `*_ENGINE` static +
`engine_for_game` dispatch arm), src/shared/types.ts (`GameId` union + `GAMES` record),
App.tsx (hardcoded valid-GameId list in the activeGame initializer), WelcomeScreen.tsx
(picker entry). At 20+ games this is unsustainable and typo-prone.

### The fix (do NOT try to remove the irreducible ~10 files - novel per-game behavior and
reverse-engineering always cost; the target is the ~15 wiring files)

- Stage 1 (backend single source of truth): introduce a `GameSpec` bundling everything for
  one game - identity (id, display names), storefront ids (the `GameDef` fields:
  executables/process_names/steam/epic/xbox), the engine config (`ModEngineConfig`, or an
  engine-family reference + params), the loader list (see loader-registry), and
  `index_game_name`. One file per game exposes its `GameSpec`; a `GAME_REGISTRY` array (or
  map) replaces the scattered statics. `engine_for_game`, `game_def_for_id`, and the
  detection loops all DERIVE from the registry. A family-conforming new game becomes: one
  new spec file + one registry line.
- Stage 1 also folds in kill-pd3-fallback: `engine_for_game` / `game_def_for_id` return
  Result/Option, and an unknown game id is a hard error, never a silent `&PD3_ENGINE`.
- Stage 3 (renderer derives from GAMES): App.tsx's valid-id list becomes
  `Object.keys(GAMES)`; WelcomeScreen iterates the `GAMES` record; per-game UI quirks
  become spec fields (e.g. `launchFlags: ['fileopenlog']` for pd3) instead of
  `activeGame === 'pd3'` conditionals in TopBar/SettingsPage. `GameId` stays
  `keyof typeof GAMES`.
- Stage 4 (behavior hooks - this is what stops the SHARED files growing per game): add
  optional hook fields to `GameSpec` for the novel 20%, so game-specific logic lives in
  that game's module instead of `game_id == "x"` branches in the big shared files -
  `archive_resolver` (Crime Boss skeleton synthesis in zip.rs), `enabled_sync` (Crime Boss
  ModSettings in crimeboss_settings.rs, UE4SS mods.txt in ue4ss_modstxt.rs),
  `embedded_id_parser` (BeardLib main.xml / RAID supermod.xml + mod.xml in identify.rs).
  Migrate opportunistically (whenever a `game_id ==` branch is touched), not big-bang.
  zip.rs is already 1176 lines and every CB special case lands there today - highest
  structural value.

Ordering: Stage 1 -> Stage 3 -> Stage 4, each behavior-preserving on top of the existing
461 tests. Coordinate with loader-registry (the loader list is a GameSpec field) and
conformance-test-suite below.

---

## TODO: loader-registry

Scalability - highest payoff-to-churn of the add-a-game work. Medium-Large. Blocked on:
nexus-prototype-merge (minor add-add conflicts in lib.rs/api.ts). Can land before or with
game-registry Stage 1.

### The problem

Each mod loader is wired as a bespoke command pair plus scattered renderer awareness.
Backend command pairs: check_superblt/install_superblt (superblt.rs),
check_pdth_overrides/install_pdth_overrides (pdth_overrides.rs), check_dahm/install_dahm
(dahm.rs), check_raid_superblt/install_raid_superblt (raid_superblt.rs), check_ue4ss
(ue4ss.rs; install goes through the normal mod flow via the UE4SS_LOADER sentinel).
Renderer: deps.ts carries hardcoded loader-id tables and per-loader logic (`loaderModIds`,
`buildLoaderModIds`, `isUe4ssLoaderId`, `ue4ssLoaderIdsFor`, `RAID_SUPERBLT_ID`,
`isRaidLoaderId`, `loaderIdsForGame`), consumed at ~4-5 UI call sites (BrowsePage,
ModDetailPage, DepsTab, healthCheck.ts, installDepCheck.ts). Adding a game's loader means
teaching all of those a new modworkshop id - the RAID merge touched 7 renderer files for
what is conceptually one table row. This is the piece that genuinely does not survive 20
games.

### The fix

- Define a `LoaderSpec { id, modworkshop_ids: &[i64], games: &[game_id], detect:
  DetectStrategy, install: InstallStrategy }`. DetectStrategy is a list of root-level marker
  files (WSOCK32.dll/IPHLPAPI.dll for SuperBLT and RAID-SuperBLT; DINPUT8.dll +
  PDTHModOverrides.dll for PDTHModOverrides; lightfx.dll for DAHM; the per-game UE4SS proxy
  DLLs). InstallStrategy is one of: `DirectUrl(url)` (DAHM's dahm.neonsynth.de, SuperBLT's
  sblt-update.znix.xyz), `ModworkshopDownload(id)` (RAID-SuperBLT
  api.modworkshop.net/mods/49744/download), or `ViaModFlow` (UE4SS - no canonical URL,
  installs through resolve_archive_download).
- Replace the five per-loader command pairs with generic `check_loader(game_id, loader_id)`
  / `install_loader(game_id, loader_id)` that dispatch over the spec's strategy. Keep the
  existing strategy IMPLEMENTATIONS (they are already correct) - just route them through the
  spec instead of hardcoded commands.
- Renderer: deps.ts's per-loader tables collapse to one lookup over the LoaderSpec list
  (expose it to the renderer as data, ideally through the typed-ipc bindings so ids are not
  restated in TS). The ~4-5 UI call sites stop being per-loader aware: "is this dependency a
  loader for this game, and is it installed?" becomes a single spec query.
- Result: a new game's loader is ONE spec entry with ZERO renderer edits. SuperBLT's
  offsite-dependency heuristic (no modworkshop page, detected by a `blt` substring in deps)
  and UE4SS's via-mod-flow oddity remain as strategy variants, not exceptions scattered
  across components.
- The loader list becomes a `GameSpec` field (game-registry) - these dovetail.
- PRESERVE every verified detail from the loader modules and .claude/rules/backend.md (the
  per-game UE4SS proxy DLL variants, the "IPHLPAPI may be the discontinued RaidBLT" note,
  DAHM/RAID full-zip extraction vs SuperBLT DLL-only). Do not lose reverse-engineered
  specifics in the generalization.

