## TODO: extract-deps-check-hook

Renderer cleanup that lowers future per-game/per-source cost. Medium. Blocked on:
nexus-prototype-merge (BrowsePage/ModDetailPage are lightly touched by the branch, and
NexusBrowsePage would otherwise become a THIRD copy).

### The problem

The dependency-warning STATE and EFFECTS are duplicated by hand across BrowsePage.tsx and
ModDetailPage.tsx - renderer.md itself records that each "has its own parallel copy of the
surrounding state/effects, kept in sync by hand" around the shared deps.ts helpers
(collectDeps / isOffsiteDep / isLoaderDep / missingRequiredDeps / offsiteDepHost). The
Nexus branch adds NexusBrowsePage.tsx, a third place this logic would be copied.

### The fix

Extract the shared dependency-check state + effects into a `useDepsCheck` hook
(src/renderer/src/hooks/) consumed by BrowsePage, ModDetailPage, and NexusBrowsePage. The
pure functions in deps.ts stay; only the React state/effect wiring around them is
deduplicated. Coordinate with loader-registry (the loader-id lookups inside this logic
simplify once loaders are declarative).

