CI hygiene. Small-Medium. Independent of the architecture work; can land any time after
nexus-prototype-merge. NOTE: the Nexus branch already fixed the open_url cmd-metacharacter
finding (it switched to rundll32) - do not re-address that.

Add mechanical enforcement for things currently guarded only by prose:
- Security dependency audit job in .github/workflows/ci.yml: run `cargo audit` (in
  src-tauri) and `pnpm audit`. As of 2026-07-17: pnpm audit is CLEAN; cargo audit flags
  quick-xml 7.5 advisories, but its only path is a BUILD dependency
  (plist -> tauri-utils -> tauri-build), not shipped runtime input - add an audit ignore
  (audit.toml or `--ignore RUSTSEC-...`) with a comment that it clears when Tauri bumps
  tauri-utils, so the job fails only on NEW or runtime advisories. Refract_MC's
  .github/workflows/security-audit.yml is a working reference for the job shape.
- CSP dual-list sync check: a small script asserting every origin in `csp` also appears in
  `devCsp` in src-tauri/tauri.conf.json (the invariant CLAUDE.md states - a missed origin
  fails silently as blank images / broken embeds). Wire into CI.
- Updater-manifest shape assertion: a CI check that the generated latest.json matches the
  shape tauri-plugin-updater expects and the endpoint in tauri.conf.json. The update
  pipeline is the "never break" invariant (a bad latest.json silently strands all users on
  the current release). Assert the release.yml "Generate latest.json" output structure.
- Optional, low priority: add scheme/shape validation to `shell_open_path`
  (launchers/mod.rs). Its only caller passes the settings-derived gamePath so it is safe
  today, but it is an unguarded command handing its argument to explorer.exe.

